==English==

===Etymology===
[[eponym|Eponym]] after [[w:Gerard Kuiper|Gerard Kuiper]], who [[theorized]] about the belt's existence.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈkaɪpər/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[Kuiper belt]] [[object]]}}

# {{context|astronomy}} A type of [[trans-Neptunian object]] (TNO) (a certain type of [[minor planet]]) that has an orbit in the Kuiper belt (between 30-50 AU) with [[inclination|inclinations]] consistent with the [[ecliptic]].

====Synonyms====
* [[KBO]]
* [[kuiperoid]]

